-# Public audio for Marr's January 23, 2004 Commission interview
+# The recorded context for the Marr timeline passage
 
-November 8, 2026 Eastern · **B129 / FAA01 / PD01–PD04**. The National Archives lists a sound-recording item for Team 8's interview with Col. Robert Marr of NEADS on **January 23, 2004**. Its date, subject, team and agency correspond to the written memorandum, which refers to a recorded interview on physical p. 1 line 28. The recording has its own National Archives identifier, **207011012**, in Record Group **148**, series **Master Files**, NAID **5952561**. The memorandum is **2610366**, box **14**, in the separate memoranda series. [Audio item](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/207011012) · [Written memorandum](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialive/66/6103/2610366/content/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00767.pdf#page=1)
+November 8, 2026 Eastern · **B129 / FAA01 / PD01–PD04**. A full local speech-recognition scan of the nine public audio files located the apparent exchange underlying the last page of the January 23, 2004 interview memorandum. A second pass on the relevant window reproduced an apparent denial of sanitizing the story, followed by a description of the purpose of assembling the slides. That distinction bears on whether the memorandum can be read as recording an admission that errors were introduced deliberately. The audio passages and their source identifiers are now independently locatable by a listener. [Public audio item 207011012](https://catalog.archives.gov/id/207011012) · [Interview memorandum 2610366, physical p. 9](https://catalog.archives.gov/medialive/66/6103/2610366/content/arcmedia/9-11/MFR/t-0148-911MFR-00767.pdf#page=9)
 
